# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout gets CRLF (the hosted runner image sets
# `core.autocrlf=true`), and this tree has 167 places where a test reads its own source with
# `include_str!` and then locates a marker in it. Sixty-three of those markers contain a newline,
# so on Windows they simply are not found and the test fails on a difference that has nothing to do
# with the behaviour under test:
#
#     registry.rs:1177           reader impl end marker present
#     seller/upstream/mod.rs:511 upstream unit-test module boundary
#
# `text=auto` leaves files git detects as binary alone, so contract artifacts and images are
# untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
